<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#first-intermediate-period">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Intermediate Period</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2181–2055 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/22nd-century-bce">22nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Intermediate Period is the era of ancient Egyptian history between the collapse of the Old Kingdom and the reunification of the country in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a>. Royal authority at Memphis faded after the Sixth Dynasty, and power passed to provincial governors and rival lines at Herakleopolis and Thebes, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mentuhotep-ii">Mentuhotep II</a> of Thebes reunited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> around 2055 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-intermediate-period.jpg" alt="First Intermediate Period" width="320" height="654" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeff Dahl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Egypt_map-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Middle Kingdom grew out of the divided Egypt of the <b>First Intermediate Period</b>, when a dynasty at Herakleopolis claimed the throne in the north and a line of Theban rulers, the Eleventh Dynasty, built up power in the south.</blockquote><a href="/empire/middle-kingdom-of-egypt">Middle Kingdom of Egypt · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>…by decades of famine and strife, the period of disunity and relative cultural decline that Egyptologists call the <b>First Intermediate Period</b>, beginning with the Seventh Dynasty; the tomb inscription of Ankhtifi, a nomarch of its early years, describes the pitiful state of the country when famine stalked the…</blockquote><a href="/empire/old-kingdom-of-egypt">Old Kingdom of Egypt · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The pyramid was likely looted as early as the <b>First Intermediate Period</b>, and Joyce Tyldesley notes evidence that it had been opened and emptied by the Middle Kingdom.</blockquote><a href="/work/great-pyramid-of-giza">Great Pyramid of Giza · Survival &amp; Rediscovery</a></li><li><blockquote>Its brief, obscure history marks the end of Old Kingdom unity and the beginning of the <b>First Intermediate Period</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/eighth-dynasty-of-egypt">Eighth Dynasty of Egypt</a></li></ul></section>
